{"id":"cf085de5-14f8-4df9-ba5a-ef6c5fa3444f","createdAt":"2026-10-26T14:38:24.011Z","batchId":"states_claude-haiku-5-5_low","approach":"html","modelId":"claude-haiku-5-5","settings":{"effort":"low"},"presetId":"states","prompt":"Two states for a file list: an empty state with an upload call to action, and an error state with a retry button.","system":"Return only the body content of an HTML page: no doctype, <html>, <head> or <body> tags, no markdown, no code fences, no prose. The page shell below is already loaded, so build with its classes and chart helper. Inline <script> is allowed for interactivity (tabs, toggles, filters); no external requests. Add a small <style> block only for what the classes cannot express, or when the request asks for a different look, colours, fonts or layout: then follow the request.\nPAGE SHELL (already loaded; do not restate it):\n- A stylesheet with these classes. Use them instead of writing CSS:\n  layout: page (centered column), stack, row, between, center, gap-sm, gap-lg, grid + cols-2|cols-3|cols-4 (responsive)\n  surfaces: card, card-title, card-desc, alert, alert-destructive, hr\n  text: h1-h4 (styled), lead, muted, small, up, down (trend colours)\n  controls: btn, btn-secondary|btn-outline|btn-ghost|btn-destructive, btn-sm|btn-lg, btn-block; label wraps input/select/textarea; label.check wraps a checkbox or radio\n  data: table (styled; td.num for numbers), badge, badge-secondary|badge-outline|badge-destructive, stat-label, stat-value, progress (inner div with style=\"width:NN%\"), avatar\n- Charts: <div data-chart='{\"type\":\"bar|line|area|pie\",\"title\":\"…\",\"data\":[{\"label\":\"W1\",\"value\":120}]}'></div> renders an SVG chart (single series, pie gets a legend). Do not draw charts yourself.\n- Light and dark mode are handled by the stylesheet.\n\nDESIGN BRIEF (applies to every UI you produce):\n- Build a complete, realistic screen, not a skeleton: a clear title and intro, grouped sections, and enough detail that it could ship.\n- Cover exactly what the request names, with no extra pages or marketing sections.\n- Use the supplied DATA in full: every field is there to be shown. Derive useful extras from it (shares, totals, deltas, rankings) instead of inventing unrelated numbers.\n- Where it fits, add status badges, trend/change figures, secondary actions, helper text, and sensible empty or edge-case copy.\n- Establish hierarchy with headings, size and weight; group related items; keep spacing and alignment consistent.\n- Make charts readable: a title, labelled axes or values, and a legend for pie charts.\n- Never use lorem ipsum or placeholder names like \"Item 1\".","systemHash":"0c16911c9564c3db3ada7a622931ee6ffc820ebf9a373996782a9f1f0fc3c98c","systemOverridden":false,"strictOutput":false,"rawOutput":"<div class=\"page stack gap-lg\">\n  <div class=\"stack gap-sm\">\n    <h1>File list states</h1>\n    <p class=\"lead\">Two reference states for the project files panel: the empty state invites the first upload, and the error state explains a failed load and offers a retry.</p>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"stack gap-sm\">\n    <h2>Empty state</h2>\n    <p class=\"muted small\">Shown when a project has no files yet.</p>\n    <div class=\"card stack gap-lg\" style=\"align-items:center;text-align:center;padding:2.5rem 1.5rem;\">\n      <div class=\"avatar\" aria-hidden=\"true\">+</div>\n      <div class=\"stack gap-sm\">\n        <h3>No files in this project</h3>\n        <p class=\"muted\">Upload designs, specs, or exports to share them with your team. Files up to 50 MB in PDF, PNG, JPG, SVG, FIG, or ZIP.</p>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"row gap-sm\" style=\"justify-content:center;flex-wrap:wrap;\">\n        <button class=\"btn btn-lg\">Upload files</button>\n        <button class=\"btn btn-outline btn-lg\">Import from link</button>\n      </div>\n      <p class=\"small muted\">Tip: drag and drop files anywhere on this panel to upload them.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n\n  <hr>\n\n  <div class=\"stack gap-sm\">\n    <h2>Error state</h2>\n    <p class=\"muted small\">Shown when the file list request fails. Previously loaded data is not displayed.</p>\n    <div class=\"card stack gap-lg\">\n      <div class=\"between\" style=\"flex-wrap:wrap;gap:0.75rem;\">\n        <div class=\"stack gap-sm\">\n          <h3>Project files</h3>\n          <p class=\"small muted\">Last successful update: 14 min ago</p>\n        </div>\n        <span class=\"badge badge-destructive\">Failed to load</span>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"alert alert-destructive stack gap-sm\">\n        <strong>We couldn't load your files.</strong>\n        <span>The server responded with 503 Service Unavailable. This is usually temporary. Your files are safe and nothing was deleted.</span>\n        <span class=\"small\">Error ID: FL-503-8842</span>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"row gap-sm\" style=\"flex-wrap:wrap;\">\n        <button class=\"btn\">Retry</button>\n        <button class=\"btn btn-ghost\">Go to project overview</button>\n        <button class=\"btn btn-ghost\">Contact support</button>\n      </div>\n\n      <p class=\"small muted\">Retrying automatically in <span id=\"retry-count\">30</span> seconds.</p>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<script>\n(function () {\n  var el = document.getElementById('retry-count');\n  if (!el) return;\n  var n = parseInt(el.textContent, 10);\n  var t = setInterval(function () {\n    n -= 1;\n    if (n <= 0) { clearInterval(t); el.textContent = '0'; return; }\n    el.textContent = String(n);\n  }, 1000);\n})();\n</script>","deltas":[[839,"<div"],[1006," class=\"page st"],[1009,"ack g"],[1009,"ap-lg\">\n  "],[1009,"<div class=\"st"],[1009,"ack g"],[1009,"ap-sm\">\n    <"],[1009,"h1>File list states</h"],[1015,"1>\n    <p class=\""],[1035,"lead\">Two"],[1064," reference states for the"],[1076," project"],[1103," files"],[1173," pan"],[1173,"el: the"],[1173," empty state inv"],[1174,"ites the"],[1197," first upload, and the error